<RCC>
    <!--
        The dock's own appearance, offered the way res/themes.qrc offers the
        ribbon themes: built in by the applications that want it rather than
        carried by the library. The images these sheets point at stay in qxdock,
        which is why the url(:/qxdock/res/images/...) paths need no rewriting.

        Two fragments, not four sheets. One look has one modifier left that a
        sheet cannot decide for itself: QX_DOCK_X11 (the only thing in the tree
        that knows which desktop this is). FocusHighlighting used to be the
        second, and cost a fragment because it is a C++ fact a style sheet
        cannot ask about - it is now a dynamic property on the widgets the rules
        name ("focused" on the panel and the tab, "focusHighlighting" on the
        title bar), so those rules travel in base.css and simply do not match
        when the flag is off. base.css is the look; x11.css is appended by
        dockStyleSheet().

        Named dockstyle rather than dock so it does not read as a theme family
        beside res/themes/: this is one look in two pieces, not two looks to
        choose from, and a DockWindow without them is unstyled rather than
        differently styled.

        prefix="/" with the directory inside each <file>, which is how
        res/themes.qrc does it and why the paths come out as
        :/dockstyle/base.css. Putting "dockstyle" in the prefix as well would
        find them at :/dockstyle/dockstyle/base.css.
    -->
    <qresource prefix="/">
        <file>dockstyle/base.css</file>
        <file>dockstyle/x11.css</file>
    </qresource>
</RCC>
